WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.708
Host: Explain why activating complement and
limiting complement are both necessary.

2
00:00:05.708 --> 00:00:10.457
Guide: Activation labels and attacks targets
and recruits responses.

3
00:00:10.457 --> 00:00:15.776
Guide: Regulation limits amplification and
terminal injury on host surfaces,

4
00:00:15.776 --> 00:00:20.264
Guide: preserving useful defense without
uncontrolled tissue damage.

5
00:00:20.264 --> 00:00:26.148
Host: Why can different complement activation
pathways have common downstream effects?

6
00:00:26.148 --> 00:00:31.181
Guide: They converge on C3 activation and
shared downstream components.

7
00:00:31.181 --> 00:00:38.415
Guide: Convergence explains shared effects
such as C3b-mediated opsonisation despite
different triggers.
